# Q5. Context Switch Overhead

## Given

Context switches = 20,000/sec

Burst Time = 2 ms

Time Quantum = 1 ms

Very high I/O frequency

---

## Root Cause

The quantum is shorter than the average CPU burst.

Each thread is preempted before completing execution.

Frequent I/O operations also trigger additional context switches.

This produces excessive scheduling overhead.

---

## Optimization 1

Increase Time Quantum

Example:

1 ms → 4 ms

This reduces unnecessary context switches.

---

## Optimization 2

Reduce I/O waits

- Buffer I/O
- Use asynchronous I/O
- Batch disk operations

---

## Benefits

- Lower context switching
- Higher CPU utilization
- Better throughput

---

## Conclusion

Short time quantum and frequent I/O cause excessive context switching. Increasing quantum and optimizing I/O significantly reduce overhead.
